Package: zfbehavior
Title: Zebrafish Larval Light-Dark Behavior and Developmental Toxicity
    Analysis with Agent Skills
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(
      person("Jui-Hua", "Hsieh", , "juihua.hsieh@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1620-1571")),
      person("Kathryn", "Konrad", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Analysis of zebrafish larval light-dark transition test
    (LDTT) tracking data and developmental toxicity in five modules: data
    import and consistency checks; raw-response visualization and
    inter-plate vehicle-control quality control; endpoint calculation
    (Total Distance, Distance Change, Distance Shift, Movement Similarity),
    normalization and intra-plate vehicle-control quality control; ANOVA
    and repeated-measures ANOVA hit calling; and Curvep-based benchmark
    concentration (BMC) modeling of behavioral and developmental toxicity
    endpoints. Ships Agent Skills that guide a coding agent or a person
    through one recorded run per step with a rendered 'Quarto' report.
    Methods follow Hsieh et al. (2019) <doi:10.1093/toxsci/kfy258>,
    Konrad et al. (2026) <doi:10.1016/j.neuro.2025.103371> and Truong
    et al. (2026) <doi:10.1016/j.neuro.2026.103504>.
